I think the trouble stems from the fact that you have the "lmerTest" package loaded, which must be taking over calls to lmer. You can either skip loading lmerTest, or you might be able to get it to work despite loading lmerTest by downloading the ezPredict source:

https://github.com/mike-lawrence/ez/blob/master/R/ezPredict.R

and modifying lines 11 & 89 to say:

if((fit_class=='mer')|(fit_class=='glmerMod')|(fit_class=='lmerMod')|(fit_class=='merModLmerTest')){

--
Mike Lawrence
Graduate Student
Department of Psychology & Neuroscience
Dalhousie University

~ Certainty is (possibly) folly ~

